\f0\fs24 \cf2 The dining room fireplace is wrapped in a fascinating legend. It is said that the entire space was designed around the discovery of this ancient hearth in a farmhouse on the outskirts of Milan. Enthralled by their find, the Bagatti Valsecchi brothers embarked on a meticulous search for Renaissance architectural and decorative elements to frame the fireplace appropriately. Among the drawings preserved in the museum archives, we can admire the design for the hood, adorned with a detached 16th-century fresco, and the lion figures carved into the vertical elements. The legend and mystery surrounding the fireplace continue to captivate us, almost as if time itself had never moved on.}